Mappings documented in the commit body without ADR-asks:
- (a) /u -> /a mapping — wrong direction; JS /u enables Unicode mode (matches Arabic digits), Perl /a is MORE restrictive than default. Worker's own comment says "no Perl analogue is exactly right" but the /a choice is the inverse of JS /u. Filed #45 as decision ADR-grow.
- (b) g and y flags tracked on object but test()/exec() single-match. Per ADR 0013, g must be honoured by test and y must be \G-anchored. Oracle proves divergence: r/x/y.test("yxy") -> false, port -> true; r/\d/g.exec stateful iteration -> 1|2|3, port -> 1|1|1 (or 1,true|1,true|1,true depending on capture shape). Filed #46 as bug.
- (c) exec prepends $& for [full, cap1, cap2, ...] shape — faithful on the corpus case (r/(.)(.)/.exec("ab") -> ab,a,b) but for no-capture-group patterns Perl 5.40 qr// in list context returns a builtin boolean which is then prepended and rendered as "true"/"false". Filed #48.
- (d) global/test return !!1/!!0 so _js_to_string routes through is_bool -> "true"/"false" — faithful, oracle pins it.

